WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.988
The reasoning patterns in this module transfer well
across SQL systems but

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.688
exact syntax can differ AND OR NOT IS NULL COALESCE
NULLIF and

00:00:09.712 --> 00:00:14.612
CASE are broadly familiar across databases IS
DISTINCT FROM is supported in

00:00:14.625 --> 00:00:18.875
PostgreSQL and some modern systems but you should
check the target platform

00:00:19.762 --> 00:00:25.600
Date arithmetic is especially variable PostgreSQL
can subtract dates directly while

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:30.512
SQL Server and Microsoft Fabric commonly use
functions such as DATEDIFF The

00:00:30.525 --> 00:00:35.212
best transfer strategy is to preserve the rule first
Define the cohort

00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:39.700
decide how NULL should behave group mixed conditions
with parentheses order CASE

00:00:39.712 --> 00:00:45.438
branches and test boundary records Translate
dialect-specific functions after the logic

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:46.100
is correct
